  "id": "animism",
  "term": "animism",
  "definition": "Animism is the belief that nature and bodily life are animated by souls, spirits, or other inner agencies. In historical accounts, it can mean everything in nature is alive, that bodies contain a distinct animating principle, or that they are inhabited by the spirits of the dead.",
